  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Original whole-organism low-poly reconstruction in resting/walking pose. Nine paired perforated dorsal-lateral sclerites above nine paired non-jointed lobopods, long limbless anterior extension. No fossil slab-only substitution. [\"Nine versus ten appendage pairs disputed historically. This version uses the newer paper’s explicitly tentative nine-pair interpretation, not a claim of certainty.\", \"Anterior identity is inferred from comparison with related lobopodians; no visible eye details are established here.\", \"Soft-body cross-section, pose and colour reconstructed. Plate hole count is deliberately simplified for low-poly viewing, not an exact microfossil reproduction.\", \"Fig2 concerns Microdictyon sp. isolated plates; use for reticulation architecture only, not exact individual plate dimensions of M.sinicum.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"representative_centerline_length_m\": 0.07, \"status\": \"Approximate representative size based on Fig1a YRCP0041 and its 10mm scale bar, not a direct specimen measurement or species maximum.\", \"estimated_trunk_diameter_m\": 0.006, \"estimated_leg_length_m\": 0.01, \"estimated_mid_sclerite_height_m\": 0.005, \"shape_dimensions_note\": \"Minor dimensions estimated from published complete fossil with compaction uncertainty; record generated dimensions rather than implying live soft-body metrics are known.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Original whole-organism low-poly reconstruction in resting/walking pose. Nine paired perforated dorsal-lateral sclerites above nine paired non-jointed lobopods, long limbless anterior extension. No fossil slab-only substitution. [\"Nine versus ten appendage pairs disputed historically. This version uses the newer paper’s explicitly tentative nine-pair interpretation, not a claim of certainty.\", \"Anterior identity is inferred from comparison with related lobopodians; no visible eye details are established here.\", \"Soft-body cross-section, pose and colour reconstructed. Plate hole count is deliberately simplified for low-poly viewing, not an exact microfossil reproduction.\", \"Fig2 concerns Microdictyon sp. isolated plates; use for reticulation architecture only, not exact individual plate dimensions of M.sinicum.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"representative_centerline_length_m\": 0.07, \"status\": \"Approximate representative size based on Fig1a YRCP0041 and its 10mm scale bar, not a direct specimen measurement or species maximum.\", \"estimated_trunk_diameter_m\": 0.006, \"estimated_leg_length_m\": 0.01, \"estimated_mid_sclerite_height_m\": 0.005, \"shape_dimensions_note\": \"Minor dimensions estimated from published complete fossil with compaction uncertainty; record generated dimensions rather than implying live soft-body metrics are known.\"}"
  },
